      "id": "bottom",
      "name": "Bottom Accretion",
      "description": "The pale field is the underside: a quarter to nearly half the horse, bounded by a single line running nose-to-tail at a third to a half of the local body depth measured up from the belly, rising a little over the shoulder and rather more over the flank. The boundary undulates gently and has no edge at all - it is a gradient a hand's span or two wide. All four legs are included the whole way to the hoof with no separate boundary of their own, and about three horses in five also take a cap on the muzzle.",
